{
  "about": "Ground-truth fixtures for measuring nutrition accuracy. Each case states the ingredients and their TRUE weights (as if weighed on a kitchen scale), plus reference macros for the meal. The harness runs the ingredients through the real resolver and arithmetic and reports MAPE per nutrient.",
  "whatThisMeasures": "Resolution and arithmetic, holding portion size constant. Reference totals are the sum of published per-100g composition at the stated weights, so a failure means the resolver matched the wrong record or the arithmetic drifted — the two regressions that would silently corrupt a health log. It does NOT measure portion estimation, which is the vision stage's job and the larger error source overall (~36% MAPE in published evaluations). For that, add cases with real photographs and scale-weighed reference values via photoPath; the harness reports those in the same table.",
  "referenceSource": "Reference macros are the USDA FoodData Central composition of the stated ingredients at the stated weights, computed independently. For regional preparations absent from FDC, values follow IFCT 2017.",
